  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Use mathematical induction to prove each of the following inequalities:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q7a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$n^2>2n$ for all $n\\ge3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True for all integers $n\\ge3$.\n\nStart at $n=3$; if $k^2>2k$, then $(k+1)^2>4k+1>2(k+1)$.",
          "worked": "Base case: $3^2=9>6=2\\cdot3$.\n\nInductive hypothesis: assume $k^2>2k$, where $k\\ge3$.\n\nInductive step:\n$$\\begin{align*}(k+1)^2&=k^2+2k+1\\\\(k+1)^2&>2k+2k+1\\\\(k+1)^2&>4k+1\\\\(k+1)^2&>2k+2\\\\(k+1)^2&>2(k+1).\\end{align*}$$\nHere $4k+1>2k+2$ because $2k-1>0$ for $k\\ge3$. Therefore, by mathematical induction, the result holds for all integers $n\\ge3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 84
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q7b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$n^n>n!$ for all $n\\ge2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True for all integers $n\\ge2$.\n\nStart at $n=2$ and use $(k+1)^{k+1}>(k+1)k^k>(k+1)k!=(k+1)!$.",
          "worked": "Base case: $2^2=4>2=2!$.\n\nInductive hypothesis: assume $k^k>k!$, where $k\\ge2$.\n\nInductive step:\n$$\\begin{align*}(k+1)^{k+1}&=(k+1)(k+1)^k\\\\(k+1)^{k+1}&>(k+1)k^k\\\\(k+1)^{k+1}&>(k+1)k!\\\\(k+1)^{k+1}&>(k+1)!.\\end{align*}$$\nThe first strict inequality uses $k+1>k>0$; the second uses the inductive hypothesis. Therefore, by mathematical induction, the result holds for all integers $n\\ge2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 84
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q7c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$n!>2^n$ for all $n\\ge4$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True for all integers $n\\ge4$.\n\nStart at $n=4$ and use $(k+1)!>(k+1)2^k>2^{k+1}$.",
          "worked": "Base case: $4!=24>16=2^4$.\n\nInductive hypothesis: assume $k!>2^k$, where $k\\ge4$.\n\nInductive step:\n$$\\begin{align*}(k+1)!&=(k+1)k!\\\\(k+1)!&>(k+1)2^k\\\\(k+1)!&>2\\cdot2^k\\\\(k+1)!&>2^{k+1}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe second strict inequality uses $k+1>2$. Therefore, by mathematical induction, the result holds for all integers $n\\ge4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      }
    ]
  },
